$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B for preparation of
MIA-phenylalanin-derivates. A mixture of acetic acid (1.5 mmol, 1.0 eq),
amine (1.8 mmol, 1.2 eq), TBTU (0.58 g, 1.8 mmol, 1.2 eq), and DIPEA
(0.66 ml, 3.75 mmol, 2.5 eq) in anhydrous DCM (0.2 M) was stirred at room
temperature overnight. Water was added and the mixture was extracted with
DCM. The combined organic layers was washed with 1N hydrochloric acid and
brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The
resulting residue was purified by silica gel flash chromatography using
10-20% ethyl acetate in hexanes. The desired amide product. 9e: Light
yellow oil, (435.9 mg, 82%). R f = 0.68, hexane/EtOAc = 4:1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ = 7.33-7.31 (m, 3H), 7.27-7.25 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.19 (m,
4H), 7.04-7.02 (m, 2H), 5.13 (d, J = 29.2 Hz, 1H), 5.09 (d, J = 29.2 Hz,
1H), 4.96-4.91 (m, 1H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 3.16-3.08 (m, 2H), 1.97 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ = 171.1, 162.6, 149.9, 135.6, 135.1, 129.3,
128.5, 128.4, 128.3, 126.9, 67.1, 62.8, 53.1, 37.9, 9.5; ESI-HRMS Calcd
for C20H23N2O4 + [M+H+]: 355.1652; Found: 355.1652. [α]26 D = -0.9
(CHCl3, c = 1.0).
