$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
compound 10a, 10d-10j, 10l-10p, 10s-10u: A mixture of 4 (1.0 equiv, each
one), amine (1.5~2 equiv), HATU (1.2 equiv) and DIPEA (2.0 equiv) in dry
DCM (2~5 mL) was stirred for 8 to 10 h at room temperature. Then the
reaction mixture was diluted with DCM (15 mL), washed with water (10
mL*2) and brine (10 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by prep-HPLC. 10a,
10d-10j, 10l-10p, 10s-10u in 9-80% yield, respectively. Compound 10p:
Yield: 1 mg, 9%. Negative ESIMS [M + Cl]- m/z 588; 1H NMR (Pyridine-d 5,
600 MHz) δ H: 7.32 (1H, d, J=8.6 Hz, H-2' and H-6'), 6.91 (1H, d, J=8.5
Hz, H-3' and H-5'), 5.07 (1H, overlapped, H-3 and H-2''), 4.59-4.53 (2H,
overlapped, H-1''a and H-3''a), 4.41-4.32 (2H, overlapped, H-1”b amd
H-3”b), 4.03-3.95 (2H, overlapped, H-11 and H-7'), 3.88 (1H, t, J=7.1 Hz,
H-8'), 3.64 (3H, s, OMe), 3.10 (1H, d, J=6.8 Hz, H-14), 2.62 (1H, dd,
J=13.2, 6.3 Hz, H-1a), 2.49 (1H, m, H-2a), 2.37 (1H, dd, J=14.5, 11.3 Hz,
H-12a), 2.18 (1H, d, J=14.2 Hz, H-12b), 2.14-2.07 (1H, m, H-2b), 1.84
(1H, d, J=12.1 Hz, H-10), 1.76-1.66 (1H, m, H-1b), 1.61-1.52 (2H,
overlapped, H-6a and H-8), 1.51 (3H, s, H-18), 1.45-1.34 (1H, m, H-7a),
1.33-1.26 (1H, m, H-7b), 1.27-1.12 (3H, overlapped, H-6b and H-16), 1.11
(3H, s, H-20), 1.03 (3H, s, H-19), 0.84 (3H, d, J=6.5 Hz, H-17); 13C NMR
(151 MHz, Pyridine-d 5) δ C: 181.0 (s,C-15), 180.3 (s, C-9'), 159.0 (s,
C-4'), 143.7 (s, C-4), 130.3 (s, C-1'), 129.4 (d, C-2' and C-6'), 121.3
(d, C-3), 114.1 (d, C-3' and C-5'), 73.7 (d, C-11), 59.2 (t, C-1''), 58.8
(t, C-3''), 58.3 (d, C-2''), 55.0 (q, OMe), 53.3 (d, C-7'), 48.4 (d,
C-14), 46.5 (d, C-10), 44.3 (s, C-13), 43.9 (s, C-9), 40.8 (d, C-8'),
39.8 (t, C-12), 38.7(s, C-5), 36.6 (t, C-6 and C-8), 28.7 (t, C-7), 26.8
(t, C-2), 22.8 (q, C-16), 20.5 (t, C-1), 19.9 (q, C-19), 18.4 (q, C-18),
17.2 (q, C-17), 14.5 (q, C-20).
